+# AF-AP-152, VERIFY-SCRUB2 F7: the lenient key-block rule retried `-{3,}` at every dash of a run and scanned to the end of
+# the text from every BEGIN head with no END (over 20 s on 60,000 dashes; 0.014 s before SCRUB2), and the Cookie rule read
+# the rest of its line from every head (2.7 s on 64,000 characters). VERIFY-SCRUB2-R1 B1: round 1's value classes read a
+# backslash run again at every pair of it (29 s on 64,000 backslashes after a Cookie head); the texts from the Cookie head
+# on hold backslash runs, escapes and heads after each changed rule's head (the escaped Cookie heads killed a stop that
+# made each head read the rest of the line; the base64 token, the Negotiate token's stops). A child times each scrub on
+# each hostile text; every call must take under 2 s (the slowest took 0.28 s in the sandbox on 2026-09-28, under load),
